==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|gera}}, {{m|non|gøra}}, {{m|non|gørva}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*garwijaną}}.

===Alternative forms===
* {{qualifier|mostly archaic}} {{l|is|gjöra}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈcɛːra/|lang=is}}
* {{rhymes|ɛːra|lang=is}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-weak|gerði|gert}}

# {{lb|is|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[do]]{{jump|is|do|s}}
#: ''Hvað ertu að '''gera'''?''
#:: What are you '''doing'''?
#: ''Letingjar '''gera''' aldrei neitt.''
#:: Loafers never '''do''' anything.
# {{lb|is|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[make]]{{jump|is|make|d|s}}
# to [[arbitrate]], to [[determine]]{{jump|is|arbitrate|d|s}}
# {{lb|is|impersonal}} ''used with nouns denoting a weather condition to indicate that that type of weather is going on''
#: ''Það '''gerði''' rigningu.''
#:: It '''rained'''.

